<ContentLayout title="Kryos OS — The foundation of Kryos" description="Kryos OS is the operating-system project at the center of the Kryos ecosystem. It is being built from scratch in Rust." heading="Kryos OS." lead="The foundation of the Kryos ecosystem. An operating system being built from scratch in Rust, with a focus on security, reliability, privacy and user choice.">
  <section class="section shell content-columns">
    <div><h2>Development status</h2><p class="content-copy">Kryos OS is an active development project. Consult the project's official release channel for verified installation availability. Do not install unofficial files claiming to be Kryos releases.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="/en/downloads/">Release availability <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a></div>
    <div><h2>Design objectives</h2><ul class="content-list"><li>A secure foundation for personal computing.</li><li>Privacy and reliability built into the system's design.</li><li>Meaningful control over applications and system behavior.</li><li>An adaptable environment for different users and needs.</li></ul></div>
  </section>
  <section class="section shell article-content">
    <h2>Part of a wider ecosystem</h2>
    <p class="content-copy">Kryos OS is the central product. Veckt is being developed as its browser companion. The system and its applications are intended to feel coherent without forcing every component to share the same release schedule.</p>
    <h2>Technical direction</h2>
    <p class="content-copy">Kryos OS is being developed in Rust, following a capability-based microkernel direction. This describes the project's architectural direction, not a promise that every planned security or isolation property is already available in a release.</p>
  </section>
</ContentLayout>